WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.491
Volume, pace, pitch, emphasis, gesture and facial expression change how an audience

00:00:05.491 --> 00:00:06.813
understands spoken words.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:12.412
What is the purpose of a full stop during oral reading? Answer: Pause and mark the

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.611
end of a sentence.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:19.229
Say a sentence as a warning and as an invitation; compare tone and expression.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:22.657
Why it works: Pausing marks the sentence ending.
